# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR, IN ONE SENTENCE: keep out the things a clone can
# rebuild, and keep in everything a reader needs to check the numbers.
#
# THE DEFAULT HERE IS TO SHIP. This repository's entire claim is that the
# documents ship WITH the tests, because a benchmark whose corpus exists only as
# URLs stops being reproducible the moment a link moves. A .gitignore that
# excluded the corpus, the renders, the manifests and both evidence files while
# tracking only the hand labels would fail NOTHING on the way out: the push
# succeeds, every file that is supposed to exist exists, and the published
# repository is a set of answers with the questions removed. IF YOU ADD A LINE
# HERE, CHECK IT WITH `git check-ignore -v <path>` AGAINST SOMETHING THAT MUST
# SHIP.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUILD OUTPUT AND DOWNLOADS. 5.8 GB, all reconstructible from the install
# scripts. These are the only things in the tree that genuinely must not ship.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
envs/
vendor/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERYTHING BELOW THIS LINE IS DELIBERATELY TRACKED. The entries are written
# out rather than left implicit so that a later edit has to argue with a
# comment before it can drop one of them.
#
# Sample_Documents/     the source documents themselves, plus PROVENANCE.txt,
#                       which states the basis on which each one may be
#                       redistributed. The documents ARE the corpus.
#
# real/sources.json     the manifest: which document, which page. Replacing a
#                       corpus is a data edit, and this is the data.
# real/pages/*.pdf      the cut page, which is what the PDF parsers read
# real/pages/*_300.png  the render, which is what the OCR floor and the hosted
#                       models read
# real/pages/*.truth.json   the hand labels and the arithmetic rules
# real/pages/index.json     what the builder detected about each page
# real/pages/cross_checks.json  the identities that run BETWEEN pages
#
#     A missing index.json or cross_checks.json does not look like damage. The
#     labels are still there, reconcile.py still reports a clean pass on what
#     it can see, and the cross-page checks simply never run. That is the
#     quietest possible failure of a repository whose subject is quiet failure.
#
# corpus/               the synthetic purchase orders, at 150 and 300 DPI. The
#                       README reports results measured on them, and the script
#                       that generated them is no longer in this repository, so
#                       these files are now the only copy. Citing results from a
#                       corpus nobody can obtain is the exact failure this
#                       project spends its length describing.
#
# out/  out_real/       every parser's raw text output, the token counts, and
#                       scores.json / reconcile.json.
#
#     THE HOSTED RUNS ARE EVIDENCE AND CANNOT BE REGENERATED. They cost money,
#     and this project's own finding is that the two hosted endpoints do not
#     return the same bytes twice. Re-running them does not reproduce these
#     numbers -- it produces different ones. The local runs are reproducible and
#     ship anyway, because 6 MB is a cheap price for letting a reader diff a
#     parser's actual output against the label it missed.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Operating-system and editor droppings, which are neither.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
